"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched on June 15th with a $500,000 budget for Phase One, led by Sarah Tan. The project team was expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Significant progress has been made, including a breakthrough in predictive analytics and the successful completion of the testing phase for a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. A detailed report on Phase Two progress will be presented on November 20th, and feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November. The project reached a milestone celebration on October 10th, with user interface enhancements planned for October. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, will be updated starting January next year. Additionally, the compliance plan's budget has been increased to $55,000."
